<!-- Handoff about.html: ahead. Native Astro markup; shared document shell is V9Layout. -->
<section class="g-white" id="ahead">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="eyebrow" data-v9-reveal><span class="tick">\</span> Where this goes</div>
    <h2 style="--d:60ms" data-v9-reveal>Four claims. Hold us to them.</h2>
    <p class="lead" style="--d:120ms" data-v9-reveal>What we want someone to be able to say about us in five years.</p>
    <ol class="ab-cl">
      <li style="--d:0ms" data-v9-reveal>
        <span class="ab-k">01</span><h3>A recruiter closes ten hires a month.</h3><div>
          <p>
            Everything we build aims at that number, by taking away the work that was never worth doing. Nobody has to
            work longer hours to get there.
          </p><span class="ab-today">Today, on technical roles: under two a month</span>
        </div>
      </li>
      <li style="--d:60ms" data-v9-reveal>
        <span class="ab-k">02</span><h3>Every interviewer has done the job.</h3><div>
          <p>
            The bench is more than fifty people. It has to grow without that sentence stopping being true, which is the
            hardest constraint in the business.
          </p><span class="ab-today">Today: true for every interview</span>
        </div>
      </li>
      <li style="--d:120ms" data-v9-reveal>
        <span class="ab-k">03</span><h3>A candidate keeps their score.</h3><div>
          <p>
            One interview that travels, owned by the person who sat it and readable by any team they release it to.
          </p><span class="ab-today">Today: part of the way there</span>
        </div>
      </li>
      <li style="--d:180ms" data-v9-reveal>
        <span class="ab-k">04</span><h3>The bar gets written down, everywhere.</h3><div>
          <p>
            Even by companies that never hire us. If structured hiring becomes ordinary and we made no money from it,
            we’d still call that the outcome we wanted.
          </p><span class="ab-today">Today: one search at a time</span>
        </div>
      </li>
    </ol>
    <p class="decide" data-v9-reveal>
      <b>Fewer people spending a year finding out they were the wrong shape for a room.</b>
    </p>
  </div>
</section>
